# Allow-list. This repo usually IS the operator's home directory (root's, on the
# Coolify host — where the Coolify web terminal and Tailscale SSH land), so only the
# deployment repo's own files are tracked. Everything else — dotfiles, the MCP token
# env file, shell history, Claude Code's sessions, other projects — stays out, and
# `git add -A` is safe.
*
!.gitignore
!.mcp.json
!AGENTS.md
!CLAUDE.md
!README.md
!instance.yaml
!skills-lock.json
!docs/
!docs/**
!stacks/
!stacks/**
